{"id":4250,"date":"2025-03-20T01:01:00","date_gmt":"2025-03-19T19:31:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/?p=4250"},"modified":"2025-03-20T01:01:00","modified_gmt":"2025-03-19T19:31:00","slug":"what-kind-of-doctor-treats-tmj-pain","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/what-kind-of-doctor-treats-tmj-pain\/","title":{"rendered":"What Kind of Doctor Treats TMJ Pain?"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>If you are asking yourself the question, \u2018What kind of doctor treats TMJ?\u2019, then\u00a0this article will help you get clarity on that. And if you are looking for a consultation to guide you in the right direction, then you can reach out to Prof. Dr. Dhivya Dilipkumar, one of India\u2019s leading and best TMJ specialists with more than 15 years of experience in the field. Call her at <a href=\"tel:+919884520520\">9884 520 520<\/a> and book an appointment right away.<\/em><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Before understanding who treats TMJ, we have to first understand the TMJ disorders. And even before that, let\u2019s first understand TMJ.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">TMJ, or Temporomandibular Joint, is the pivotal hinge that connects the temporal bones of your skull, which are situated just in front of the ears and your jaw. It lets you move your jaw up and down and side to side, allowing you to talk, chew and yawn.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now that we are familiar with TMJ let\u2019s take a look at TMJ disorders. TMJ disorders can cause pain in your jaw joint and in the muscles that control jaw movement. These disorders can be caused by various factors, including Stress , long dental procedure , genetics, arthritis, or jaw injury.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Some people who suffer from TMJ disorders may also tend to clench or grind their teeth (bruxism). The pain and discomfort with TMJ disorders may be temporary or last for a longer period of time. It is known to be more prevalent in women than in men and is most common among individuals aged 20 to 40.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Symptoms of TMJ:<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/tmj-symptoms-and-treatment\/\" data-type=\"link\" data-id=\"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/tmj-symptoms-and-treatment\/\">Symptoms of TMJ disorders<\/a> can include:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Pain or tenderness in the jaw<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Aching pain in and around your ear<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Difficulty chewing or discomfort while chewing<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Aching facial pain<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Vertigo , Ear Stuffiness , Tinnitus<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>At times pain radiating to teeth &#8211; teeth may feel sensitive or painful<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Locking of the joint, making it difficult to open or close your mouth<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>A clicking sound or grating sensation when opening your mouth or chewing.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Tigtness feeling &nbsp;in the throat<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Understanding TMJ Disorders<\/strong><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The Anatomy of the TMJ<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The TMJ is one of the most complex joints in the body because of its capability of forward and backward movement, rotations, and side-to-side movements. TMJ is unique in its composition and function; it is made up of the mandibular condyles, which fit into the temporal bone&#8217;s glenoid fossa.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The parts of the bones that interact in the joint are covered with cartilage and are separated by a small shock-absorbing disk, which usually keeps the movement smooth.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Types of TMJ Disorders<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">TMJ disorders can generally be divided into three categories:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\" start=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Myofascial Pain:<\/strong>&nbsp;This is the most common form of TMJ Disorder, which involves discomfort or pain in the muscles that control jaw function as well as the neck and shoulder muscles.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Internal Derangement of the Joint:<\/strong>&nbsp;This category includes a displaced disc, a dislocated jaw, or injury to the condyle, the rounded ends of the jaw bone.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Degenerative Joint Disease:<\/strong>&nbsp;This includes osteoarthritis or rheumatoid arthritis in the jaw joint.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Factors Contributing to TMJ Disorders<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Several factors can contribute to the development of TMJ disorders:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Trauma to the jaw or temporomandibular joint can lead to these disorders.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>The habit of grinding or clenching teeth can put a lot of pressure on the TMJ.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Different types of arthritis, such as rheumatoid arthritis and osteoarthritis, can affect the TMJ.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Stress can cause a person to tighten facial and jaw muscles or clench the teeth.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Chronic neck and upper back muscle strain can affect the TMJ by altering the muscle function and placing more strain on the TMJ.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Diagnosing TMJ Disorders<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Diagnosing TMJ disorders involves a detailed medical history and physical examination. Your healthcare provider will discuss your symptoms and examine your jaw. They will listen to and feel your jaw when you open and close your mouth, observe the range of motion in your jaw, and press on areas around your jaw to identify sites of pain or discomfort.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Initial Examination: What to Expect<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">During the initial examination, your healthcare expert might:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Ask you to bite down to check the alignment of your teeth.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Check for areas of tenderness or swelling.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use a stethoscope to listen for clicking, popping, or grating sounds during jaw movement.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Diagnostic Tools and Tests for TMJ<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Further tests may be ordered to help rule out other conditions and confirm the diagnosis:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>X-rays: To examine bones and joints and possibly to rule out other conditions.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI): To view the soft tissue, including the TMJ disc and surrounding muscles. This can help determine if the disc is in the proper position as your jaw moves.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Computed Tomography (CT) Scan: To provide detailed images of the bones involved in the joint.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>TMJ Arthroscopy: In some cases, a minimally invasive procedure called arthroscopy may be used. A small thin tube (cannula) is placed into the joint space, and an arthroscope is then inserted to view the area and to help diagnose a TMJ disorder.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Top 10 Types of Doctors Who Can Treat TMJ<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now that we are familiar with TMJ, TMJ disorders, and the various tools and tests, let\u2019s take a look at the kind of doctors that will help you treat TMJ.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1. General Dentists<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/\">General dentists<\/a> are often the first and the most common healthcare professionals to be consulted for TMJ disorders due to their expertise with the conditions affecting the mouth and jaw. A dentist experienced in TMJ disorders can provide initial care and treatment and guide you in case some other niche expert has to be consulted.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Role of a Dentist in TMJ Disorders<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Diagnosis: General dentists can diagnose TMJ disorders based on your symptoms, dental and medical history, and a clinical examination.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Management: They can offer management strategies for TMJ disorders, including medications, bite guards, and referrals to specialists if necessary.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Oral Splints or Mouth Guards: Often used for people who clench or grind their teeth. These devices can help alleviate muscle tension and protect the teeth and jaw from further damage.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Physical Therapy: Including exercises to strengthen and stretch the jaw muscles.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Medications: Non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) to relieve pain and muscle relaxants to ease muscle tension.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">2. Oral and Maxillofacial Surgeons (OMS)<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/oral-and-maxillofacial-surgery\/\">Oral and maxillofacial surgeons<\/a> specialize in surgical treatments related to the face, mouth, and jaw. They are trained to address complex TMJ disorders, especially those requiring surgical intervention.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">&nbsp;<strong>When to Consult an OMS<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Refer to an OMS if:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Conservative treatments have failed to relieve your symptoms.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>There is significant structural damage to the joint.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>The disorder has resulted in severe limitations in jaw function.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Surgical Options for TMJ Treatment<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Arthrocentesis: A minimally invasive procedure where small needles are inserted into the joint so fluid can be used to wash out the joint. This can remove debris and inflammatory byproducts.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>TMJ Arthroscopy: Similar to arthrocentesis but with a small scope used to view inside the joint space. Minor surgeries can be performed with instruments inserted through additional small incisions.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Open-Joint Surgery: If the joint&#8217;s structural integrity is compromised, more invasive surgery may be required to repair or replace the joint.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>OMS may also recommend non-surgical treatments, such as injections of corticosteroids into the joint to reduce inflammation or Botox injections to relieve muscle tension.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">3. Orthodontists<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/orthodontics\/\" data-type=\"link\" data-id=\"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/orthodontics\/\">Orthodontists<\/a> are experts in correcting irregularities of the teeth and jaw, including issues related to alignment and bite, which can impact TMJ disorders. Their expertise in mouth structure and jaw makes them an ideal consultant for TMJ disorder management.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>How Orthodontic Treatment Can Help with TMJ Disorders<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Correcting Bite Issues:<\/strong>&nbsp;Malocclusions, or misalignments of the teeth, can contribute to TMJ disorders by creating uneven stress on the jaw. Orthodontic treatments like braces or Invisalign can correct these bite irregularities, potentially relieving TMJ symptoms. Dr. Dhivya and her team specialize in Invisalign, and have a holistic approach to both consultation and treatment.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Realigning the Jaw:<\/strong>&nbsp;In some cases, more advanced orthodontic procedures may be necessary to realign the jaw and alleviate pressure on the TMJ.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Braces, Aligners, and Other Orthodontic Appliances<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Braces:&nbsp;<\/strong>Traditional braces can be used to move the teeth into better alignment, which may help alleviate TMJ symptoms caused by bite issues.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Invisalign:<\/strong>&nbsp;Offers a less visible option for correcting bite and alignment issues that may contribute to TMJ disorders.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Palatal Expanders:<\/strong>&nbsp;For some patients, widening the upper jaw with a palatal expander can relieve TMJ symptoms by creating a more favorable bite relationship.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>4<\/strong>. <strong>TMJ Specialists<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/tmj-specialist-in-chennai\/\" data-type=\"link\" data-id=\"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/tmj-specialist-in-chennai\/\">TMJ specialists<\/a> are not a specific type of healthcare provider but rather are general dentists, oral surgeons, or other types of doctors who have expertise and interest in treating TMJ disorders. They may have more experience with TMJ disorders than other practitioners.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Criteria for Seeing a TMJ Specialist<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Persistent Symptoms:<\/strong>&nbsp;If TMJ symptoms persist despite initial treatments, a TMJ specialist can offer more advanced care.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Complex Cases:<\/strong>&nbsp;For complex or severe TMJ disorders, specialists can provide comprehensive treatment plans that may include a combination of therapies.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Advanced Treatments and Therapies Offered by TMJ Specialists<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Custom Oral Appliances:<\/strong>&nbsp;Beyond standard splints or mouthguards, TMJ specialists may offer custom-designed oral appliances for better effectiveness.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Advanced Imaging and Diagnostics:<\/strong>&nbsp;Specialists might utilize more sophisticated imaging techniques to understand the intricacies of your condition.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Multidisciplinary Approaches:<\/strong>&nbsp;TMJ specialists often work closely with a team of healthcare providers, including physical therapists, pain specialists, and others, to address TMJ disorders from multiple angles.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">5. Physical Therapy for TMJ Management<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Physical therapy can be an effective treatment for TMJ disorders, focusing on exercises to improve jaw movement, strengthen jaw muscles, and relieve pain.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Role of Physical Therapy in TMJ Treatment<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Improving Mobility:<\/strong>&nbsp;Physical therapists can teach exercises to improve the mobility of the jaw and reduce stiffness.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Reducing Pain:<\/strong>&nbsp;Techniques such as heat or cold therapy, ultrasound, and electrical stimulation can help reduce pain and inflammation.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Exercises and Manual Therapies for TMJ Relief<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Jaw Exercises:<\/strong>&nbsp;Specific exercises can help stretch and strengthen the jaw muscles, increasing mobility and reducing symptoms.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Manual Therapy:<\/strong>&nbsp;Physical therapists may use hands-on techniques to gently mobilize the jaw joints and muscles, improving function and reducing pain.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Physical therapy for TMJ disorders typically involves a personalized treatment plan tailored to the individual&#8217;s specific symptoms and needs. This may include home exercises, in-office treatments, and education on how to manage symptoms and prevent further jaw strain.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">6. Chiropractic Care for TMJ Disorders<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Chiropractic care focuses on diagnosing and treating mechanical disorders of the musculoskeletal system, especially the spine. Some chiropractors also apply these principles to the temporomandibular joint, using:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Manual Adjustment:<\/strong>&nbsp;Gentle manipulation of the jaw to improve alignment and mobility.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Soft Tissue Therapy:<\/strong>&nbsp;Techniques to relax and stretch the muscles around the jaw, reducing tension and pain.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Acupuncture:&nbsp;<\/strong>This traditional Chinese medicine technique involves inserting thin needles into specific points on the body. For TMJ disorders, it can help relieve pain and reduce muscle tension around the jaw.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Massage Therapy:<\/strong>&nbsp;Focusing on the muscles of the neck, shoulders, and face can help alleviate the muscle tightness associated with TMJ disorders, promoting relaxation and pain relief.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">7. Pain Management Specialists<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Pain management specialists are experts in diagnosing and treating pain that is more severe or complex, including chronic pain associated with TMJ disorders. They employ a variety of strategies to alleviate pain and improve quality of life.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Approaches to Managing Chronic TMJ Pain<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Medication Management:<\/strong>&nbsp;This may include prescription pain relievers, muscle relaxants, or even antidepressants that can help reduce pain levels.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Injection Therapies:<\/strong>&nbsp;Techniques such as trigger point injections or Botox injections into the jaw muscles can provide significant relief from TMJ-related pain.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Corticosteroid Injections:<\/strong>&nbsp;Injecting steroids into the TMJ can reduce inflammation and pain for some patients.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Botox Injections:<\/strong>&nbsp;Although primarily known for cosmetic uses, Botox can be injected into the jaw muscles to temporarily relieve pain by reducing muscle tension.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">8. Psychological Support for TMJ Sufferers<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">TMJ disorders can have a significant impact on one&#8217;s quality of life, often leading to stress, anxiety, and even depression. Psychological support can be a crucial component of a comprehensive treatment plan.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>The Impact of TMJ Disorders on Mental Health<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Chronic pain and limited jaw function can affect daily activities, leading to frustration and emotional distress. It&#8217;s essential for patients and healthcare providers to recognize and address these psychological aspects.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Behavioral Therapy and Stress Management Techniques<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Cognitive-Behavioral Therapy (CBT):<\/strong>&nbsp;This form of psychotherapy helps patients change negative thought patterns and behaviors that may contribute to their pain and dysfunction.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Stress Management:<\/strong>&nbsp;Techniques such as meditation, deep breathing exercises, and biofeedback can help reduce the stress that often exacerbates TMJ symptoms.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Incorporating psychological support into TMJ disorder treatment acknowledges the complex interplay between physical symptoms and emotional well-being, offering a more holistic approach to patient care.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">9. Lifestyle Modifications and Home Remedies<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Making certain adjustments to daily habits and incorporating home remedies can significantly alleviate the symptoms of TMJ disorders. These changes can help manage pain, improve jaw function, and possibly prevent further aggravation of the condition.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">&nbsp;<strong>Self-care Practices for TMJ Relief<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Jaw Rest:<\/strong>&nbsp;Minimizing extreme jaw movements, such as wide yawning, loud singing, and chewing gum, can help relieve TMJ strain.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Heat and Cold Packs:<\/strong>&nbsp;Applying warm compresses can improve blood flow and relax the jaw muscles, while cold packs can reduce inflammation and numb pain.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Gentle Jaw Stretching and Relaxation Exercises:<\/strong>&nbsp;Simple exercises can help increase jaw mobility, reduce stiffness, and decrease pain. It&#8217;s important to perform these exercises gently and within a range of motion that doesn&#8217;t cause pain.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Dietary Changes and Exercises to Manage TMJ Symptoms<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Soft Food Diet:<\/strong>&nbsp;Switching to softer foods can help minimize jaw movement and allow the TMJ to rest and heal.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Avoiding Hard, Crunchy, and Chewy Foods:<\/strong>&nbsp;These types of foods can exacerbate TMJ pain and should be avoided or minimized.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Mindful Eating Habits:<\/strong>&nbsp;Eating smaller bites and chewing slowly can help reduce the strain on the TMJ during meals.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The Future of TMJ Treatment<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Advancements in medical science and technology continually provide new insights into the diagnosis and treatment of TMJ disorders. Research is ongoing, and the future of TMJ treatment looks promising, with potential for innovative therapies.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Emerging Treatments and Research<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Regenerative Medicine:&nbsp;<\/strong>Techniques such as stem cell therapy and platelet-rich plasma (PRP) injections are being explored for their potential to regenerate damaged tissues in the TMJ.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Neuromodulation:<\/strong>&nbsp;Using electrical stimulation to modulate nerve activity and alleviate pain is another area of research that may offer new solutions for TMJ disorders.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The Role of Technology in Diagnosing and Treating TMJ Disorders<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Advanced Imaging Techniques:<\/strong>&nbsp;Developments in imaging technology, such as 3D imaging and functional MRI, provide more detailed views of the TMJ, aiding in accurate diagnosis and tailored treatments.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Customized Treatment Approaches:<\/strong>&nbsp;Computer-aided design (CAD) and computer-aided manufacturing (CAM) technologies enable the creation of customized oral appliances with a precise fit, enhancing treatment effectiveness.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Temporomandibular Joint (TMJ) disorders encompass a range of conditions that can cause pain and dysfunction in the jaw joint and muscles controlling jaw movement. While the causes for TMJ disorders can vary a lot, the treatment always begins by understanding the disorders in and out. This can help you choose the right treatment, the right medical consultant, and the right approach.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">All this begins with the right kind of consultant to help you in the complex space of TMJ disorder pain management. Prof. Dr. Dhivya Dilipkumar is one of India\u2019s leading TMJ specialists and has been treating and guiding patients for TMJ disorders for years. For more than 15 years, she and her team, with a very customer-centric approach, have been giving relief to many patients suffering from TMJ disorders.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It is very important for people experiencing TMJ disorders to actively participate in the process of pain relief by seeking and following the right advice among the various treatment options available. With TMJ disorders, the goal is not just to reduce the pain but also to prevent any complications that may arise in the future.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The process and the path to managing TMJ disorders are as unique as the patients themselves. While the medical community is trying its best to ensure each patient gets the best treatment, there is constant R&amp;D going on in the medical and dental care space for more effective treatments. These will surely improve the quality of life for the patients and help them approach the journey with a lot more confidence.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Until then, take care and Godspeed!<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">FAQs:<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Who is the best TMJ specialist in India?<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Prof. Dr. Dhivya Dilipkumar is one of the best <a href=\"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/tmj-specialists-in-india\" data-type=\"link\" data-id=\"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/tmj-specialists-in-india\">TMJ specialists in India<\/a> with more than 15 years of experience in the field. You can reach out to her at <a href=\"tel:+919884520520\">9884 520 520<\/a> and book a consultation with her.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>What causes TMJ disorders?<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">TMJ disorders can be caused by a variety of factors, including jaw injury, arthritis, genetic predisposition, excessive jaw clenching or teeth grinding, and misalignment of the teeth or jaw.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>How do I know if I have a TMJ disorder?<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Common symptoms include pain or tenderness in the jaw, aching pain around the ear, difficulty or discomfort while chewing, locking of the joint, and a clicking or grating sound when opening the mouth or chewing.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Can TMJ disorders go away on their own?<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Some TMJ disorder symptoms can improve without treatment. However, if your symptoms persist or cause significant discomfort, it is important to seek medical advice.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>What are the treatment options for TMJ disorders?<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Treatment options range from conservative self-care practices, such as jaw exercises and stress management, to medical treatments like medication, physical therapy, and dental splints. In severe cases, surgical interventions may be considered.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>If you are asking yourself the question, \u2018What kind of doctor treats TMJ?\u2019, then\u00a0this article will help you get clarity on that. And if you are looking for a consultation to guide you in the right direction, then you can reach out to Prof. Dr. Dhivya Dilipkumar, one of India\u2019s leading and best TMJ specialists [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[48],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-4250","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-tmj"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/4250","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/drdilipdentalcentre.com\/wp-js